.\" man/man3/Docv::Manpath.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Manpath" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Manpath \- The manual search path, and lookup of pages along it.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Manpath\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The manual search path, and lookup of pages along it.
.PP
A root is a tree of \fB\%man<section>\fR directories (\fB\%/usr/share/man\fR), or a
flat directory with pages in it (a project\(aqs \fB\%doc/\fR). \fB\%Manpath.default\fR
puts the man page directories of the current project first, then the
directories added with \fB\%docv \%path\-add\fR (\fB\%read_paths\fR), then the
system path as man\-db builds it (\fB\%system\fR). It also holds the
project\(aqs Markdown documents (\fB\%Project#documents\fR).
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
manpath = Docv::Manpath.default(Dir.current)
manpath.find("printf", "3") # => "/usr/share/man/man3/printf.3.gz"
.EE
.RE
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBCONFIGS = ["/etc/man_db.conf", "/etc/manpath.config"]\fR
man\-db configuration files, the first existing one is read.
.TP 4
\fBDEFAULTS = ["/usr/share/man", "/usr/local/share/man", "/usr/man"]\fR
The mandatory directories when there is no man\-db configuration.
.TP 4
\fBMARKERS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
MARKERS = [".git", ".hg", ".svn", ".jj", "shard.yml", "Cargo.toml", "package.json", "go.mod", "pyproject.toml", "setup.py", "Gemfile", "pom.xml", "build.gradle", "CMakeLists.txt", "meson.build", "configure.ac", "Makefile", "makefile"] of ::String
.EE
.RE
.PP
Files and directories that mark the root of a project.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBMAX_DEPTH = 4\fR
Levels below the project root searched for pages.
.TP 4
\fBMAX_DIRS = 2000\fR
Directories looked at in one project at most.
.TP 4
\fBNEIGHBORS = ["../man", "man", "../share/man", "share/man"]\fR
Directories tried next to a \fB\%PATH\fR element without a \fB\%MANPATH_MAP\fR
line, as man\-db does.
.TP 4
\fBORDER\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ORDER = ["1", "n", "l", "8", "3", "0", "2", "3type", "3posix", "3pm", "3perl", "3am", "5", "4", "9", "6", "7"] of ::String
.EE
.RE
.PP
Section search order (man\-db\(aqs default), then all other sections.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBPATHS_FILE = "paths"\fR
The file of directories added with \fB\%docv \%path\-add\fR.
.TP 4
\fBPATHS_HEADER\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
PATHS_HEADER = "# Man page directories added with docv path\-add, one per line.\en"
.EE
.RE
.RE
.TP 4
\fBSECTION = /\eA(?:[0\-9][a\-zA\-Z0\-9]*|n|l)\ez/\fR
A section name: \fB\%1\fR, \fB\%3p\fR, \fB\%3type\fR, \fB\%n\fR, \fB\%l\fR.
.TP 4
\fBSKIP\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
SKIP = Set {"node_modules", "vendor", "lib", "target", "__pycache__"}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Directories not searched for a project\(aqs pages, besides hidden ones.
.RE
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.default(dir : String | Nil = nil) : Manpath\fR
The search path of the \fB\%docv\fR command: the man page directories of
the project around \fIdir\fR (\fB\%project\fR; none when \fB\%nil\fR), the added
directories (\fB\%read_paths\fR), then the system path (\fB\%system\fR), with the
project\(aqs documents.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.new(roots : Enumerable(String), locale : String | Nil = Manpath.locale, project : Project | Nil = nil)\fR
The search path of \fIroots\fR in order, each a tree or flat directory
(\fB\%Manpath.flat?\fR); missing and repeated directories are dropped. The
roots among the pages of \fIproject\fR are marked \fB\%Root#project\fR.
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.absolute(dir : String) : String\fR
\fIdir\fR as an absolute path (\fB\%\(ti\fR expanded).
.TP 4
\fBdef self.add_paths(dirs : Array(String), file : String = paths_file) : Array(String)\fR
Adds \fIdirs\fR, made absolute, to \fIfile\fR; returns those it did not hold.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.discover(dir : String) : Array(String)\fR
The man page directories of the project around \fIdir\fR
(\fB\%project\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef self.flat?(dir : String) : Bool\fR
True for a directory with pages in it and no \fB\%man<section>\fR
directories.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.locale : String | Nil\fR
The message locale from the environment, \fB\%nil\fR for C/POSIX.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.locale_variants(locale : String | Nil) : Array(String)\fR
Locale directory names to try, most specific first: \fB\%nl_NL.UTF\-8\fR,
\fB\%nl_NL\fR, \fB\%nl\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.man_db(files : Array(String) = CONFIGS) : ManDb\fR
The man\-db configuration from the first of \fIfiles\fR that exists; with
none, no maps and \fB\%DEFAULTS\fR as the mandatory directories.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.page?(path : String) : Bool\fR
True for a file named like a page (\fB\%split\fR) whose text, gzip or not,
starts with a roff control character.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.pages?(dir : String) : Bool\fR
True for a directory with man pages: a tree or a flat directory.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.parse_man_db(text : String) : ManDb\fR
Reads the \fB\%MANPATH_MAP\fR and \fB\%MANDATORY_MANPATH\fR lines of a man\-db
configuration.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.parse_reference(text : String) : Tuple(String, String | Nil)\fR
Parses \fB\%name(sec)\fR references; returns \fB\%{name, \%section}\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.paths_file : String\fR
The file of added directories: \fB\%$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/paths\fR, or
\fB\%\(ti/.config/docv/paths\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.project(dir : String) : Project | Nil\fR
The project around \fIdir\fR (\fB\%project_root\fR) with its man page
directories (trees and directories with pages) and its Markdown
documents (\fB\%Markdown.file?\fR, not hidden), found breadth\-first up to
\fB\%MAX_DEPTH\fR levels and \fB\%MAX_DIRS\fR directories below the root,
skipping hidden directories, \fB\%SKIP\fR and symbolic links. A tree is not
searched further. \fB\%nil\fR without a project root.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.project_root(dir : String) : String | Nil\fR
The project root around \fIdir\fR: the nearest directory from \fIdir\fR up
that holds one of \fB\%MARKERS\fR, below the home directory; without one,
\fIdir\fR itself unless it is the home directory or \fB\%/\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.rank(section : String) : Tuple(Int32, String)\fR
Sort key of a section in search order: its place in \fB\%ORDER\fR (sections
not listed come last), then its name.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.read_paths(file : String = paths_file) : Array(String)\fR
The added directories, one per line of \fIfile\fR; lines starting with
\fB\%#\fR are comments.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.remove_paths(dirs : Array(String), file : String = paths_file) : Array(String)\fR
Removes \fIdirs\fR, made absolute, from \fIfile\fR; returns those it held.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.split(file : String, section : String = "") : Tuple(String, String) | Nil\fR
Splits a page file name into name and section: \fB\%printf.3.gz\fR is
\fB\%{"printf", \%"3"}\fR. In a section directory (\fIsection\fR given) the
extension must start like the section; elsewhere it must be a section
name (\fB\%SECTION\fR). \fB\%nil\fR for other files.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.system(manpath : String | Nil = ENV["MANPATH"]?, path : String | Nil = ENV["PATH"]?, config : ManDb = man_db) : Array(String)\fR
The system search path as man\-db builds it (manpath(5)): \fImanpath\fR
(\fB\%MANPATH\fR) with each empty component standing for the default path,
or else the default path: for each element of \fIpath\fR (\fB\%PATH\fR) its
\fB\%MANPATH_MAP\fR directories, or the \fB\%NEIGHBORS\fR that exist, then the
\fB\%MANDATORY_MANPATH\fR directories.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef all_sections : Array(String)\fR
All sections across the roots, in search order.
.TP 4
\fBdef find(name : String, section : String | Nil = nil) : String | Nil\fR
Finds the file of \fIname\fR, in \fIsection\fR when given (a section prefix like
\fB\%3\fR also matches \fB\%3p\fR, \fB\%3type\fR). Sections go in search order, roots in
path order within each.
.TP 4
\fBdef project : Project | Nil\fR
The project whose pages and documents come first, if any.
.TP 4
\fBdef roots : Array(Root)\fR
The roots in search order; the locale subdirectories of a tree come
before it.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/manpath.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Manpath::ManDb" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Manpath::Project" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Manpath::Root" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Markdown" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
